    "message": "Run a tick's phases in Rust when no hook watches them\n\nrules/tick.rs runs the phases in order, calling kernels directly and each\nPython part through one entry. TickEngine.step asks controller.run_tick\nfirst; a trace, a callable Provider, a shadow or a patched step or rule refuse\nbefore anything changes, and the phases run through phase_handler as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
